----------------------------------------------------------------------
FastJet
-------

The FastJet package provides a fast implementation of the
longitudinally invariant kt jet finder as introduced in

  S.~Catani, Y.~L.~Dokshitzer, M.~H.~Seymour and B.~R.~Webber,
  Nucl.\ Phys.\ B {\bf 406}  (1993)  187.

and 

  S.~D.~Ellis and D.~E.~Soper,
  Phys.\ Rev.\ D {\bf 48} (1993) 3160 [hep-ph/9305266]. 

The implementation is based on the geometrical methods described in
hep-ph/0512210.

Installation instructions are provided in the INSTALL file.

Note that to benefit from NlnN implementation of the jet finder you
will need to download CGAL, from http://www.cgal.org/ and compile it
before compiling the fastjet library.

Automatic documentation can be generated by running the doxygen command 
(if not installed on your system see www.doxygen.org) in the main 
directory. It will  create the html/ and latex/ directories containing 
detailed technical documentation.

Directory structure
-------------------

doc/		Documentation
src/		the .cc files for the FastJet library
include/	the include (.hh) files for the FastJet library
lib/            destination for the libfastjet.a library
example/        contains some example programs
data/           contains some files with data for events

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Known bugs
----------

With the NlnN strategies, on events with many particles with identical
kt values, the clustering hangs. The detailed reason has yet to be
understood, but it may be connected with the std::map being used.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
DEBUGGING:
example/fastjet_timing -verbose 2 -r 0.72  -strategy -3 -write -incl 5.0 < ../data/single-event.dat

This hangs for unknown reason (strategy=-2 case also has problems, but
not identical). Running with valgrind reveals no problems (but might
not expect problems to show up?). Just before it hangs (step 373) it
tries to recombine a particle that's already been recombined. But it
also misclusters particle 362 immediately after its creation (step
363).

Another problem is that ktjet_example has wrong behaviour for
r/=1.0. This too needs to be understood...

